From: Andreas Baierl <ichgeh@imkreisrum.de>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:20:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Ignore key repeats for keys that open or close views

A single short press of kInfo could open the detail view and close it
again immediately, because remotes / CEC frequently deliver an additional
repeat event (k_Repeat) for the same key. Since ProcessKey() masked out
k_Repeat, this repeat was treated like a second press and closed the
just opened detail view.

Only react to the initial key press for kInfo, kBlue, kOk, kBack and kRed.
Navigation keys keep their repeat behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EteH3QmdLhyMzBxYeCwjve
---
 tvguideosd.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tvguideosd.c b/tvguideosd.c
index d4c19c1..4c2d439 100644
--- a/tvguideosd.c
+++ b/tvguideosd.c
@@ -632,6 +632,19 @@ eOSState cTvGuideOsd::ProcessKey(eKeys Key) {
     eOSState state = osContinue;
     cPixmap::Lock();
     bool alreadyUnlocked = false;
+    // Keys that open or close a view must only react to the initial key press.
+    // Otherwise a repeat event of the same key (sent by many remotes / CEC
+    // even for a single short press) immediately closes the just opened view
+    // or reopens a just closed one.
+    if (Key & k_Repeat) {
+        switch (Key & ~k_Repeat) {
+            case kInfo: case kBlue: case kOk: case kBack: case kRed:
+                cPixmap::Unlock();
+                return state;
+            default:
+                break;
+        }
+    }
     if (detailView) {
         //Detail View Key Handling
         switch (Key & ~k_Repeat) {
